Looks like it's time for me to check out the endgame.  Got 2 articles
called "Amulet of Yendor":  I _knew_ it was too easy on level 35, so I
went down to level 50 instead and am now working my way back to the top.

From recent discussions, I gather at some point there is a special
sequence to go through... but the object of the game is the same, right?
Get to level 1 and go up?  Not take some detour on a hell level.

Obligatory dumb question:  Is there any use for figurines?  I've found
interesting things to do to statues, but not figurines.

Obligatory opinion:  The people who get discouraged when they die in
silly ways are missing the point.  If you are swinging a cockatrice,
that overbalances the game in your favour.  Of course there are
corresponding risks.  What I do is:

- Genocide 'em as soon as possible
- Be cautious around bones levels, these aren't hard to identify
- In particular, levitate almost all the time.  This has some added
  benefits, like avoiding pits, landmines, and trapdoors, as well as any
  nasty cockatrice corpses.

As for incu/succubi, my experience indicates (maybe falsely) they don't
do much when you're blind.  So while wielding a cockatrice it's better
to be a nearsighted, airborne adventurer.  (Maybe "glasses" might be a
good new game object -- blessed glasses of far vision and cursed glasses
of smudge (similar to potion of hallucination).)

